          "lineNumber": 2,
          "issue": "Removed verify(rawBody, signature) check allows any caller to supply arbitrary rawBody and signature, causing markPaid to be invoked without authenticating the webhook. This violates the documented contract and enables attackers to mark orders paid fraudulently.",
          "suggestion": "Re‑introduce signature verification before processing the payload. For example:\n```\nif (!verify(rawBody, signature)) {\n  throw new Error(\"invalid signature\");\n}\nconst event = JSON.parse(rawBody);\nreturn markPaid(event.orderId);\n```\nEnsure verify is called with the raw request body and that errors are handled appropriately.",
